  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-02-11T21:59:24.938Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently, on live, it is possible to see a significant portion of someone's chatbox over the main menu. If you wanted to browse your avatars or find a new world to hop to, it was possible to still see what they were saying if they were unable to speak at the time. You'd also be in a position where you're still looking mostly at the person.\n\nHowever, on beta, almost all of the top margin is now taken up. You could point your camera at the ceiling and use the bottom margin, but from the other person's PoV, you're no longer looking at them and able to see their chatbox.\n\nI think a good and simple solution to this would be to lower the menu and re-center it, so the bottom and top margins are the same again. EDIT: Per the VRChat Discord, the room at the bottom of the menu is to accommodate three lines of tooltips. So, the only other thing I can think of currently would be to allow the menu to be resized. Or perhaps add a button to collapse/expand the new menu header, as is done with the wings.\n\nI phrase this as an accessibility concern because you can still hear someone talking to you behind the main menu. If the person in front of you was muted when you pulled up the main menu and was un-muted when the menu was dismissed, this would be very inconvenient. For someone who physically cannot speak without using a chatbox, this is essentially what's happening to them now.\n\nI've included screenshots of the difference.",
